INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'sbi-chief-ai-officer-6-posts-20261105', 'global', 'India',
'SBI Chief AI Officer Recruitment 2026: 6 AI Leadership Posts, Apply by 16 November',
'',
'State Bank of India has extended the deadline for SBI Chief AI Officer recruitment 2026 to 16 November 2026, with six senior AI posts on fixed-term contracts.',
'',
$$<p>State Bank of India has extended the deadline for SBI Chief AI Officer recruitment 2026, covering six senior artificial intelligence posts, to 16 November 2026. A corrigendum dated 4 November 2026 moved the closing date from 9 November 2026. The recruitment, run by the bank's Central Recruitment and Promotion Department under advertisement CRPD/SCO/2026-27/30, covers a General Manager and Chief AI Officer, three Deputy General Managers, and two AI architects. The bank said the corrigendum also revises the qualifications for the General Manager and Deputy General Manager posts and the experience required for two posts, so anyone who read the original advertisement dated 19 October 2026 should check the revised notice before applying.</p>
<p>Read the limits first. The bank said candidates must be Indian citizens, and each candidate may apply for only one of the six posts; if a candidate applies for more than one, only the last valid completed application will be kept and the other fees will be forfeited. The engagement is on a fixed-term contract, not a permanent bank job, and the top post needs more than 15 years of experience, including senior leadership time in artificial intelligence and analytics.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance</th><th>Details</th></tr><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>State Bank of India, Central Recruitment and Promotion Department, Corporate Centre, Mumbai</td></tr><tr><td>Advertisement</td><td>CRPD/SCO/2026-27/30, dated 19 October 2026; corrigendum dated 4 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Posts</td><td>6 Specialist Cadre Officer posts, one vacancy each, all unreserved</td></tr><tr><td>Application window</td><td>19 October 2026 to 16 November 2026 (extended from 9 November 2026)</td></tr><tr><td>Fee payment last date</td><td>16 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application fee</td><td>Rs. 750 for General, EWS and OBC; nil for SC, ST and PwBD</td></tr><tr><td>Eligibility cut-off date</td><td>30 September 2026 for age, qualification and experience</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>Annual cost-to-company upper range Rs. 160 lakh for the General Manager post, Rs. 120 lakh for Deputy General Manager posts, Rs. 90 lakh for architect posts</td></tr><tr><td>Tenure</td><td>Fixed-term employment for 3 years, renewable for a further 2 years, up to 5 years in total</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Mumbai, or anywhere in India if the bank requires it</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Shortlisting, interview, and cost-to-company negotiation</td></tr><tr><td>Application mode</td><td>Online only, through the State Bank of India careers portal</td></tr></table>
<h2>SBI Chief AI Officer recruitment 2026: the six posts</h2>
<p>The headline post is the General Manager and Chief AI Officer, with one vacancy and an annual cost-to-company upper range of Rs. 160 lakh. The bank said the post holder will lead machine learning, artificial intelligence, natural language processing and parsing tools, design big-data workflow systems including an enterprise AI platform for generative and agentic AI, and oversee an independent model validation team. The three Deputy General Manager posts each carry one vacancy and an upper range of Rs. 120 lakh a year, covering Risk and Operational Analytics, AI Governance and Compliance, and Data Engineering, Model Application Development and AI Operations. The two architect posts each carry one vacancy and an upper range of Rs. 90 lakh a year: the AI Solution Architect and the Enterprise AI Architect, who governs the bank's enterprise AI architecture including its on-premises NVIDIA-based AI platform.</p>
<h2>Who can apply for the SBI Chief AI Officer posts</h2>
<p>For the General Manager post, the age must be between 40 and 55 years as on 30 September 2026, with a B.E., B.Tech or M.Tech in a computing or electronics branch, or an M.Sc, M.A., M.Stat or MCA. The bank said the post needs more than 15 years of experience in banking, financial services or information technology, including at least 3 years of senior leadership experience in artificial intelligence, analytics, model oversight, governance and business transformation, leading a sizeable team. Individual contributor experience does not count towards those leadership years. For each Deputy General Manager post, the age must be between 35 and 50 years with the same degree list, and more than 10 years of experience including at least 2 years in a senior leadership role in its own area. For the two architect posts, the age must be between 30 and 45 years, with a bachelor's or master's degree in a related discipline and at least 8 years of overall experience including at least 3 years in the relevant architecture work.</p>
<p>The bank said training and teaching experience will not be counted, and candidates serving in government offices, public sector undertakings, nationalised banks or financial institutions must produce a no-objection certificate from their employer at the interview. Candidates against whom there are adverse reports on character and antecedents, or on moral turpitude, are not eligible. The bank said the cost-to-company figure is an upper range and is negotiable, split into 90 per cent fixed pay and 10 per cent variable pay linked to performance. The engagement is for 3 years, renewable for a further 2 years up to 5 years in total.</p>
<h2>How to apply for SBI Chief AI Officer recruitment 2026</h2>
<p>Start on the State Bank of India careers portal and find the Specialist Cadre Officer recruitment under advertisement CRPD/SCO/2026-27/30. Register online to generate a provisional registration number and password, then fill in the form with educational, professional and personal details. The bank said saved details can be edited up to three times before final submission. Upload the photograph, signature, biodata, resume, identity and age proof, educational and experience certificates, salary slips or Form-16, and the cost-to-company negotiation sheet in the prescribed sizes and formats. Pay the fee online by 16 November 2026: Rs. 750 for General, EWS and OBC candidates and nil for SC, ST and PwBD candidates, and the bank said it is non-refundable. Submit the form, then print the application form and the e-receipt. No hard copy needs to be sent by post.</p>
<p>Selection has three stages. The bank said shortlisting comes first, and meeting the minimum eligibility does not guarantee an interview call. Shortlisted candidates then face an interview carrying 100 marks, and candidates for the General Manager and Deputy General Manager posts must also deliver a 10-minute presentation on their job profile, projects or milestones. The bank said the final merit list follows interview score alone, with ties broken by age in descending order, and cost-to-company negotiation follows at or after the interview. Outstation candidates called for interview will be reimbursed economy-class air fare for the General Manager and Deputy General Manager posts, and up to Rs. 15,000 in total for the architect posts. Apply only through the bank's own careers portal: the bank does not take applications through agents.</p>
<h2>What to do next</h2>
<p>First, read the corrigendum dated 4 November 2026 in full. Second, pick only one post and check your age, degree and leadership years against 30 September 2026. Third, gather the salary and experience documents early. Readers tracking other bank recruitment may want <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/sbi-security-officer-60-posts-20261104">State Bank of India security officer recruitment for 60 posts</a>, <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/bob-wms-837-posts-20261104">Bank of Baroda Wealth Management Services recruitment for 837 posts</a>, which closes on 24 November 2026, and <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/nicl-graduate-apprentice-200-posts-20261104">National Insurance Company apprentice recruitment for 200 posts</a>, which closes on 18 November 2026.</p>
<p><small>Sources: State Bank of India, advertisement CRPD/SCO/2026-27/30 dated 19 October 2026 and corrigendum dated 4 November 2026, as summarised by FreeJobAlert at https://www.freejobalert.com/articles/sbi-recruitment-2026-gm-chief-ai-officer-dgm-3074384 and by GovtJobsAlert at https://govtjobsalert.in/sbi-sco-ai-officer-recruitment-2026/; applications through the State Bank of India careers portal at https://sbi.bank.in/web/careers/current-openings. The advertisement states the posts, pay, dates, fee, and selection process quoted here; interview dates have not been announced.</small></p>
$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://www.freejobalert.com/articles/sbi-recruitment-2026-gm-chief-ai-officer-dgm-3074384','https://govtjobsalert.in/sbi-sco-ai-officer-recruitment-2026/','https://sbi.bank.in/web/careers/current-openings'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'co-operative-bank-kenya-ai-jobs-11-posts-20261105', 'global', 'Kenya',
'Co-operative Bank Kenya AI Jobs: 11 AI, Data and Security Roles, Apply by 9 November',
'',
'Co-operative Bank of Kenya has listed 11 AI, data, security and commercial vacancies, with most AI and data roles closing on 9 November 2026.',
'',
$$<p>Co-operative Bank Kenya AI jobs are open again, with Co-operative Bank of Kenya listing 11 vacancies across its artificial intelligence, data, cybersecurity and commercial teams, with most AI and data roles closing on 9 November 2026. The bank's own careers pages carry the postings, and applications go by email with an application letter and a detailed curriculum vitae, quoting the job reference in the subject line. Two security roles close on 11 November 2026, while the Commercial Manager for Youth Financial Services role closes on 5 November 2026, so that one needs same-day action.</p>
<p>Read the limits first. These are roles with a bank in Kenya, and the postings do not state a salary for any of the 11 roles. The postings do not mention visa sponsorship or relocation support, so readers outside Kenya should confirm work authorisation before applying. Applications go only by email to the address the bank publishes, with the role's reference number in the subject line. There is no online application form, and no fee is mentioned.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance</th><th>Details</th></tr><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Co-operative Bank of Kenya, ICT and Innovations team and related functions</td></tr><tr><td>Vacancies</td><td>11 roles</td></tr><tr><td>AI and data roles deadline</td><td>9 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Security roles deadline</td><td>11 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Commercial Manager deadline</td><td>5 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application mode</td><td>Email with application letter and detailed curriculum vitae</td></tr><tr><td>Application email</td><td>jobs@co-opbank.co.ke, with the job reference as the subject</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>Not stated in the postings</td></tr><tr><td>Work location</td><td>Kenya; no separate city is stated for each role</td></tr></table>
<h2>Co-operative Bank Kenya AI jobs: the AI and data roles</h2>
<p>The AI Integration Engineer, reference AI-IE/IID/2026, joins the bank's ICT Innovations team to design, develop and operate secure integrations connecting artificial intelligence models, agents and data solutions with core banking systems, digital channels and payments. The bank said the role needs a bachelor's degree in a related field, at least four years of experience in systems integration, API engineering, middleware, messaging or backend engineering, and hands-on experience integrating high-availability enterprise systems.</p>
<p>The Data Engineer, reference DE/IID/2026, builds the data pipelines and data products behind the bank's analytics and artificial intelligence work, including batch, streaming and real-time pipelines and support for generative AI applications. The bank said the role needs a bachelor's degree in a related discipline, at least four years of relevant experience, strong SQL skills and proficiency in Python or Scala.</p>
<p>The AI and Data Architect, reference AIDA/IID/2026, reports to the Head of Artificial Intelligence and sets the architecture for the bank's artificial intelligence and data ecosystem. The bank said the role needs a bachelor's degree in a related field and at least eight years of experience, including at least three years designing artificial intelligence, machine learning or advanced analytics solutions. The separately listed AI Data Architect, reference AI Data-A/IID/2026, focuses on enterprise data platforms, data models and governance, and needs at least seven years of experience including at least three years in data architecture or senior data modelling.</p>
<p>The AI Application Engineer, reference AI Application-E/IID/2026, designs, builds, deploys and supports AI-powered applications across the bank's customer channels and internal systems, including conversational assistants, AI agents and intelligent document processing. The bank said the role needs a bachelor's degree in a related field and at least five years of software or application engineering experience, including work with AI or generative AI. The Data Scientist, reference DS/IID/2026, works on credit, fraud detection, collections and banking operations, and needs a bachelor's degree in a quantitative field, at least four years of relevant experience, and proficiency in Python or R and SQL.</p>
<p>The AI Risk and Compliance Specialist, reference AIRCS/IID/2026, reports to the Head of Artificial Intelligence and runs the bank's responsible AI governance framework, including risk and impact assessments. The bank said the role needs a bachelor's degree in a related field and at least six years of relevant experience. The AI Quality Assurance Automation Engineer, reference AIQA-AE/IID/2026, assures the quality, safety and reliability of AI-enabled solutions, and needs a bachelor's degree in a related field and at least four years of quality assurance experience, including at least two years of hands-on test automation.</p>
<h2>The two security roles closing on 11 November 2026</h2>
<p>The Applications and Infrastructure Security Officer, reference AISO/IID/2026, protects the bank's technology infrastructure, business applications, information and digital services, managing tools such as web application firewalls, anti-malware systems, data loss prevention, endpoint encryption, privileged access management and multi-factor authentication. The bank said the role needs a bachelor's degree in a related discipline, or a business degree supported by relevant IT security qualifications, plus recognised cybersecurity certifications.</p>
<p>The ICT Security SOC Analyst, reference SOC/IID/2026, works in the bank's Security Operations Centre, monitoring networks and systems around the clock, triaging alerts and supporting incident response. The bank said the role needs a bachelor's degree in a related field, at least one year of experience in a related technical position, and a CEH or CySA+ certification as a mandatory requirement.</p>
<h2>The commercial role closing on 5 November 2026</h2>
<p>The Commercial Manager for Youth Financial Services, reference CM/YFS/2026, drives the commercial performance and growth of an assigned youth customer portfolio, covering acquisition, activation, engagement and retention. The bank said the role needs a bachelor's degree in a related discipline and at least five years of relevant experience in commercial management, go-to-market strategy, business growth, marketing, partnerships or business development. Because the deadline is 5 November 2026, this role cannot wait for the weekend.</p>
<h2>How to apply for Co-operative Bank Kenya AI jobs</h2>
<p>Prepare an application letter and a detailed curriculum vitae, then send them by email to jobs@co-opbank.co.ke with the exact job reference for the role as the subject line. The bank said candidates interested in more than one position should follow the instructions for each role, so send a separate application for each role. Check the reference before sending, since the references differ by only a few letters.</p>
<p>Apply only through the bank's own careers pages and the published email address. The postings mention no fee, so anyone asking for payment to secure one of these roles is not acting for the bank. Readers outside Kenya should also confirm, before applying, whether the bank will consider applicants who need work authorisation, since the postings do not state a position on sponsorship. Readers weighing other technology hiring may want <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/periscope-labs-senior-applied-ai-engineer-dhaka-20261104">Periscope Labs senior applied AI engineer role in Dhaka</a>, <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-training-jobs-software-engineers-20261104">AI training jobs for software engineers</a>, and <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/dubai-government-jobs-expats-45-roles-20261104">Dubai government jobs open to expatriates</a>.</p>
<p><small>Sources: Co-operative Bank of Kenya careers pages for the AI Integration Engineer at https://www.co-opbank.co.ke/careers/co-op-bank/ai-integration-engineer/, the AI Application Engineer at https://www.co-opbank.co.ke/careers/co-op-bank/ai-application-engineer/, the AI and Data Architect at https://www.co-opbank.co.ke/careers/co-op-bank/ai-data-architect-ref-aida-iid-2026/, the AI Quality Assurance Automation Engineer at https://www.co-opbank.co.ke/careers/co-op-bank/ai-qa-automation-engineer/ and the AI Data Architect at https://www.co-opbank.co.ke/careers/co-op-bank/ai-data-architect/, as compiled by Opportunities for Young Kenyans at https://opportunitiesforyoungkenyans.co.ke/2026/11/03/11-vacancies-open-at-co-operative-bank-2/. The postings state the roles, references, deadlines and application route quoted here; pay is not stated in the postings.</small></p>
$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://opportunitiesforyoungkenyans.co.ke/2026/11/03/11-vacancies-open-at-co-operative-bank-2/','https://www.co-opbank.co.ke/careers/co-op-bank/ai-integration-engineer/','https://www.co-opbank.co.ke/careers/co-op-bank/ai-application-engineer/','https://www.co-opbank.co.ke/careers/co-op-bank/ai-data-architect-ref-aida-iid-2026/','https://www.co-opbank.co.ke/careers/co-op-bank/ai-qa-automation-engineer/','https://www.co-opbank.co.ke/careers/co-op-bank/ai-data-architect/'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'nhidcl-senior-associate-25-posts-20261105', 'global', 'India',
'NHIDCL Senior Associate Recruitment 2026: 25 Posts in Delhi, Apply by 19 November',
'',
'NHIDCL has opened applications for 25 Senior Associate posts at its New Delhi headquarters, with the window running to 19 November 2026.',
'',
$$<p>The National Highways and Infrastructure Development Corporation Limited (NHIDCL) has opened NHIDCL Senior Associate recruitment 2026 for 25 Senior Associate posts at its New Delhi headquarters under Recruitment Notice No. 08/2026, dated 4 November 2026. The online window on the NHIDCL Resource Pool Portal runs from 5 November 2026 at 5 p.m. to 19 November 2026 at 3 p.m., and the interview is set for 26 November 2026. The engagement is under the corporation's Young Professionals scheme, which is a fixed-term consultancy arrangement rather than a regular staff appointment.</p>
<p>Read the limits first, because two of them will rule out many applicants. The corporation said every area needs a mandatory minimum of two years, or 730 days, of relevant post-qualification experience in the National Highways Sector, with documentary proof showing the organisation and the exact period, and general experience cannot substitute for it. The engagement is purely contractual: selected candidates work as independent consultants, not as NHIDCL staff or employees, for a fixed term of 2 years extendable by 1 year up to a maximum of 3 years. The upper age limit is 45 years as on 4 November 2026, and the notice prints no category-wise reservation breakup and mentions no application fee.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance</th><th>Details</th></tr><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>National Highways and Infrastructure Development Corporation Limited (NHIDCL), a Central public sector undertaking under the Ministry of Road Transport and Highways</td></tr><tr><td>Notice</td><td>Recruitment Notice No. 08/2026, dated 4 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Posts</td><td>Senior Associate under the Young Professionals scheme, 25 posts</td></tr><tr><td>Application window</td><td>5 November 2026 at 5 p.m. to 19 November 2026 at 3 p.m.</td></tr><tr><td>Interview</td><td>26 November 2026, reporting at 9:30 a.m.</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>NHIDCL Headquarters, New Delhi</td></tr><tr><td>Remuneration</td><td>Consolidated consultancy fee of Rs. 80,000 to Rs. 1,50,000 per month</td></tr><tr><td>Tenure</td><td>2 years, extendable by 1 year up to a maximum of 3 years</td></tr><tr><td>Age limit</td><td>Maximum 45 years as on 4 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application fee</td><td>Not mentioned in the notice</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Interview, document verification and background verification; no written examination is mentioned</td></tr><tr><td>Application mode</td><td>Online only, through the NHIDCL Resource Pool Portal</td></tr></table>
<h2>NHIDCL Senior Associate recruitment 2026: the four areas</h2>
<p>The Technical area holds the largest share, with 15 of the 25 posts. The corporation said Senior Associate (Technical) needs a degree in Civil Engineering from a recognised university or institute, and preference will be given to candidates holding a master's degree or equivalent in Civil Engineering, Structural Engineering, Construction Management or other relevant allied disciplines. With 15 seats, this is the area where candidates holding documented National Highways work have the widest opening.</p>
<p>The remaining 10 posts are split across three specialist areas. Senior Associate (Human Resources) has 4 posts and needs an MBA in Human Resources or an equivalent qualification. Senior Associate (Legal) has 3 posts and needs an LLB or LLM, or a graduate or postgraduate degree in Law. Senior Associate (Information Technology) has 3 posts and needs a B.E. or B.Tech in Computer Science, Information Technology, Networks or Electronics and Communication, or an M.Tech in Cyber Security or Network Management, or an MCA. The corporation said the number of vacancies may increase or decrease depending on requirements, and it may cancel the process at any stage without assigning reasons.</p>
<h2>Experience, age and pay for NHIDCL Senior Associates</h2>
<p>All four areas need between 2 and 9 years of relevant post-qualification experience, including the mandatory minimum of two years in the National Highways Sector. The corporation said the experience proof must show the organisation and the exact period, so applicants should gather appointment letters, experience certificates and any other documents that prove the sector and the dates before starting the form. The upper age limit is 45 years as on 4 November 2026, and the notice does not print a minimum age or a category-wise age relaxation table.</p>
<p>The pay is a consolidated monthly consultancy fee, not a salary with allowances. The corporation said the range for Senior Associates is Rs. 80,000 to Rs. 1,50,000 per month, set under the approved scheme and approved by the competent authority based on post-qualification experience. The printed experience slabs run from Rs. 80,000 per month for up to 3 years of experience, through Rs. 98,000 for 5 to 6 years, to Rs. 1,22,000 for above 9 years. The corporation said the fee is calculated by weighting National Highways Sector experience at full value and other organisation experience at 0.65, and the fee is inclusive of all applicable taxes, with no other facility or allowance payable. An annual enhancement of 5 per cent is allowed under the scheme, payment is made monthly within 7 days after completion of the month subject to certification by the controlling officer, tax is deducted at source, and the consultant is liable for goods and services tax as applicable.</p>
<h2>How to apply for NHIDCL Senior Associate recruitment 2026</h2>
<p>Start on the NHIDCL Resource Pool Portal, which opens for this notice on 5 November 2026 at 5 p.m. The portal allows registration at any time, but the application for this notice must be submitted inside the window, which closes on 19 November 2026 at 3 p.m. Register or log in, update the profile if needed, and complete the application form for this recruitment, taking care to enter the eligibility details, especially the National Highways Sector experience proof, exactly as the documents show. No fee payment step is printed in the notice, so do not pay anyone who claims to collect a fee for this recruitment.</p>
<p>Keep the email address used in the application active and unchanged for one year, since the corporation said all correspondence is only by email and no change of email address is allowed after submission. The interview takes place on 26 November 2026 at the NHIDCL Corporate Office on the 1st and 2nd floors of Tower A, World Trade Centre, Nauroji Nagar, New Delhi, with reporting at 9:30 a.m. Bring original documents plus self-attested copies, and five printed copies of the portal application, since the corporation said the interview is subject to document verification and final engagement depends on successful background verification. Canvassing or external influence will disqualify a candidate, and furnishing inaccurate, wrong, incomplete or misleading information may lead to rejection.</p>
<p>Do not submit before the portal link for this notice is active, and do not leave the form to the last hour: the window closes at 3 p.m. on 19 November 2026, not at midnight. If anything in the form is unclear, the corporation said correspondence is only by email to the helpdesk address given in the notice, and other modes are not valid. Readers tracking other Delhi and public sector openings may want <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/bob-wms-837-posts-20261104">Bank of Baroda Wealth Management Services recruitment for 837 posts</a>, <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/gsssb-cce-1237-posts-20261104">Gujarat subordinate services combined competitive examination for 1,237 posts</a>, and <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/dsssb-delhi-court-641-posts-20261104">Delhi district courts recruitment for 641 posts</a>.</p>
<p><small>Sources: National Highways and Infrastructure Development Corporation Limited, Recruitment Notice No. 08/2026 dated 4 November 2026, as summarised by SahisarkariJobs at https://www.sahisarkarijobs.in/job/nhidcl-senior-associate-recruitment-2026/; applications through the NHIDCL Resource Pool Portal at https://www.nhidcl.com/application/login and updates on the NHIDCL current vacancies page at https://www.nhidcl.com. The notice states the posts, pay, dates, experience rule, and interview arrangement quoted here; no application fee is mentioned in the notice.</small></p>
$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://www.sahisarkarijobs.in/job/nhidcl-senior-associate-recruitment-2026/','https://www.nhidcl.com/application/login','https://www.nhidcl.com'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

